ctions route by the same context -- `:store-put`\n1349:    (and the `:vm/store-put` effect) writes the active module\n1350:    store, and `:store-get` reads it, falling through to the\n1394:### 7.4 Transitive requires and cycles\n1415:## 8. The manifest registry\n1417:### 8.1 The module manifest\n1537:### 8.2 The name environment and its authority\n1664:### 8.3 What `yin.vm.module` becomes\n1730::stores {addr encoded}}}` -- the portable act-1 encoding, never\n1739:## 9. Migration from `yin.vm.debruijn-linker`\n1836:applies its export correctly; a `:store-put` executed inside an\n1857:## 10. File box\n1909:## 11. Completion criteria\n2020:    `x` through a direct `:store-put` instruction is visible to a\n2039:## 12. Open decisions\n2085:## 13. Reconciliation record\n2087:### 13.1 Revision r7 (round 6, `gpt-6-sol`)\n2106:|                                   | (7.3 grow-only returns, criterion |\n2108:| Store routing was free reads      | Agreed. The active-store context  |\n2109:| only; direct `:store-put`/        | now routes direct store           |\n2110:| `:store-get` wrote ambient state, | instructions (`:store-put` writes |\n2112:| transitive dependency stores      | `:store-get` reads it, ambient    |\n2135:### 13.2 Revision r6 (round 5, `gpt-6-sol`)\n2184:### 13.3 Revision r5 (round 4, `gpt-6-sol`)\n2223:### 13.4 Revision r4 (round 3, `gpt-6-sol`)\n2269:### 13.5 Revision r3 (round 2, `gpt-6-sol`)\n2328:### 13.6 Revision r2 (round 1, `gpt-5.6-sol`)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
