sertions refuse `:ambiguous-name`; snapshot advance). Then:\n  1805\tthe manifest and derivation\n  1806\tformat records; `register-host-module` with profile enforcement;\n  1807\t`require-handler` minting, parking, and emitting; the two wait states\n  1808\tthrough `check-wait-set` with id correlation; the install child in the\n  1809\tscheduler with the section 7.3 phases; `link-module`; the UCF table\n  1810\tamendments. Tests, per backend: a require of an unlinked module over\n  1811\tring buffers completes and the program resumes with its exports bound;\n  1812\ta manifest declaring a different name is `:module-name-mismatch`; a\n  1813\tmanifest whose semantic, H, or R derivation leads from a different tree\n  1814\tis `:derivation-mismatch` (three swapped-image tests, and a fourth\n  1815\twhere the `:yin.ast/code` tree is not the manifest's tree); a\n  1816\tsame-named primitive of different profile at the receiver is\n  1817\t`:unresolved-free`; a shadowed export name in the requiring program's\n  1818\tstore is `:shadowed-free`; a free name the manifest never declares is\n  1819\t`:undeclared-free`; two outstanding requires on one response stream\n  1820\teach restore on their own id; a response landing before the entry would\n  1821\thave been polled is not skipped; a module requiring another links\n  1822\ttransitively while a third task keeps running; a require cycle is\n  1823\t`:require-cycle`; a module that binds a name and exports a closure\n  1824\treading it links, the closure reads the module's value in the\n  1825\tparent, a parent binding of the same name neither supplies nor\n  1826\tshadows it, and a write from one export is visible to the next\n  1827\tapplication in the same task and to no other task; a read inside a\n  1828\tbody applied before its definition retains its obligation and is\n  1829\t`:undeclared-free` unless the manifest declares it; an export-only\n  1830\timage with no application site produces no obligations; a parked\n  