90\t          yin.vm.ledger (derive-record, verify-derivation)\n  1891\t          yin.vm.debruijn-code, yin.vm.debruijn-register-code\n  1892\tMust not change:\n  1893\t          image-hash, register-hash, segment-key, the opcode\n  1894\t          tables, dao.stream, dao.jing. No kernel's step function\n  1895\t          changes its decode, dispatch, or register model; the\n  1896\t          behavioral amendments r6 and r7 make at a kernel are\n  1897\t          closure-directed resolution and store routing, the\n  1898\t          :store-of consult and its frame threading (7.3).\n  1899\t```\n  1900\t\n  1901\t`yin.vm.linker` exports: `fetch`, `verify`, `discharge`, `link-state`,\n  1902\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon`, `publish!`, `ast-format`,\n  1903\t`semantic-format`, `stack-format`, `register-format`, `manifest-format`,\n  1904\t`record-format`, the four free-name, definition, and application-site\n  1905\tscanners, `row-local-defect`, `index-from-datoms`, `address-attribute`,\n  1906\t`trusted-fallback`, `verifying-fallback`, `refused`, `refused?`, `ok?`,\n  1907\t`refusal-reasons`.\n  1908\t\n  1909\t## 11. Completion criteria\n  1980\t    restore identities, and every register the loader would have reset\n  1981\t    is unchanged; the parked entry predates the attach, its recorded\n  1982\t    image is a row of the offset table, no restore writes `:segment`\n  1983\t    from an entry, and `:hash` is never a restore key; on the\n  1984\t    register backend, an image attached by a nested require while a\n  1985\t    call is in flight survives the callee's return: no frame carries\n  1986\t    or restores `:segment` or `:hash`, and the caller resumes in the\n  1987\t    grown code space at the same absolute `:return-pc`; a\n  1988\t    continuation lifted after an attach and lowered into a fresh\n  1989\t    kernel places every pc by the receiving offset table; two\n  1990\t    waiters holding images of different lengths each lower the same\n  1991\t    slice against their own coordinates and apply the export\n  1992\t    correctly.\n  1993\t18. Under `:derivation :verifying`, a manifest whose record names a\n  1994\t    profile the linker does not implement is `:unverified-derivation`,\n  1995\t    never installed; under `:trusted` the same manifest installs with\n  1996\t    `:trust :composition` in the outcome.\n  1997\t19. A request naming a mismatched contract is refused with no content\n  1998\t    request appended and no validator run.\n  1999\t20. A closure re-exported from a transitive dependency lifts with that\n  2000\t    dependency's image as origin, the parent loads that image before\n  2001\t    lowering, and an origin the scheduler never verified is\n  2002\t    `:foreign-image`; a positional marker offered to a named kernel is\n  2003\t    `:binding-mismatch`.\n  2004\t21. An exact duplicate of a valid envelope, appended any number of\n  2005\t    times, is honored exactly once and never marks its principal as\n  2006\t    equivocating; a replayed envelope with an old sequence, an envelope\n  2007\t    at or below a principal's floor, two distinct envelopes with one\n  2008\t    sequence, a retraction naming no assertion, and a retraction by\n  2009\t    another principal are each discarded with the stated kind; a\n  2010\t    retraction bound to an assertion's id removes that assertion only.\n  2011\t22. One four-way manifest links through all four kernels with no\n  2012\t    `:contract-mismatch`; a manifest of another schema version is\n  2013\t    `:descriptor-defect` with rule `:schema`; a derivation without a\n  2014\t    contract entry is `:descriptor-defect` with rule\n  2015\t    `:contract-missing`.\n  2016\t23. On every backend, a module that binds `(def x 1)` and exports a\n  2017\t    closure reading `x` links, and the closure applied in the parent\n  2018\t    reads the module's `x`, while a parent binding of the same name\n  2019\t    neither supplies nor shadows it; a write the closure makes to\n  2020\t    `x` through a direct `:store-put` instruction is visible to a\n  2021\t    sibling export applied afterwards in the same task and to no\n  2022\t    other task's module store; the same module linked by two tasks\n  2023\t    holds two isolated stores; a slice whose exports reach a\n  2024\t    dependency's store transitively carries that dependency's\n  2025\t    snapshot, including a mutation the child made through the\n  2026\t    dependency's closure, a missing snapshot is\n  2027\t    `:yin.k/non-portable` with `:yin.k/kind :missing-module-store`,\n  2028\t    and a receiving task that already holds the dependency's store\n  2029\t    keeps its own instance; a module closure calling another\n  2030\t    module's closure routes each body's reads and writes to its own\n  2031\t    module; in the child, a closure re-exported from a dependency\n  2032\t    reads that dependency's module store, not the child's ambient\n  2033\t    bindings; a walker closure whose body node sits under two\n  2034\t    `:lambda` rows with different params lifts from its recorded\n  2035\t    source row, and a fabricated closure with no recorded row\n  2085\t## 13. Reconciliation record\n  2086\t\n  2087\t### 13.1 Revision r7 (round 6, `gpt-6-sol`)\n  2088\t\n  2089\tThe round-6 review closed the dominance and scanner item (no\n  2090\taction), left two partial findings, and added one relocation edge.\n  2091\tEach, and what r7 did:\n  2092\t\n  2093\t| Item                              | Resolution                        |\n  2094\t|-----------------------------------|-----------------------------------|\n  2095\t| Register return frames restored   | Agreed. One rule now covers every |\n  2096\t| a saved `:segment` and `:hash`,   | transition: no frame, entry, or   |\n  2097\t| discarding an image attached by   | restore assigns a code-space      |\n  2098\t| a nested require mid-call         | value. The register frame drops   |\n  2099\t|                                   | `:segment` and `:hash` and its    |\n  2100\t|                                   | return restores registers only;   |\n  2101\t|                                   | the stack and semantic returns    |\n  2102\t|                                   | already conform; a lift derives   |\n  2103\t|                                   | a frame pc's image row from the   |\n  2104\t|                                   | offset table at lift time. Test:  |\n  2105\t|                                   | attach-during-call, then return   |\n  2106\t|                                   | (7.3 grow-only returns, criterion |\n  2107\t|                                   | 17, M4).                          |\n  2108\t| Store routing was free reads      | Agreed. The active-store context  |\n  2109\t| only; direct `:store-put`/        | now routes direct store           |\n  2110\t| `:store-get` wrote ambient state, | instructions (`:store-put` writes |\n  2111\t| and the slice carried no          | the active module store;          |\n  2112\t| transitive dependency stores      | `:store-get` reads it, ambient    |\n  2113\t|                                   | only for engine-filed resource    |\n  2114\t|                                   | cells) and threads across calls:  |\n  2115\t|                                   | a frame records the caller's      |\n  2116\t|                                   | active `:store-of`. The slice     |\n  2117\t|                                   | carries one snapshot per module   |\n  2118\t|                                   | reached transitively, including   |\n  2119\t|                                   | the child's mutations through a   |\n  2120\t|                                   | dependency's closures; a missing  |\n  2121\t|                                   | snapshot refuses the lift; lower  |\n  2122\t|                                   | instantiates what the task lacks  |\n  2123\t|                             